# Lab first, production only on request

This site has two tracks:

- **lab** → https://joshualisky-lab.vercel.app — experiments
- **main** → https://joshualisky.vercel.app — production

## Always

1. Work on the `lab` branch.
2. Commit and push to `origin/lab` so the lab URL updates.
3. Stop there. Tell the user what changed and that it is on lab. Give the lab URL.
4. Wait. Do not merge to `main`, push `main`, or retarget `joshualisky.vercel.app` unless the user explicitly asks to deploy / 배포 / 메인에 올려.

## Deploy (only when asked)

Then, and only then:

1. Merge `lab` into `main` and push `origin/main`.
2. Point `joshualisky.vercel.app` at the new production deployment. That hostname does not always follow new production deploys on its own — re-alias it after the deploy is READY.
3. Point `joshualisky-lab.vercel.app` at the latest lab deployment if it also stuck.

## Do not

- Ship a homepage or nav experiment straight to `main` because it “looks done”.
- Treat “메인에서 …” as git `main`. In this project that usually means the homepage. Git production is only when they say 배포.
- Mix 밥도둑 into this site’s home. Keep it as a separate hobby link.
